meta {
  name: Search Remittances
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/remittances?accountId={{senderAccountId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
}

params:query {
  accountId: {{senderAccountId}}
  ~status: COMPLETED
  ~from: 2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
  ~to: 2026-12-31T23:59:59.999Z
  ~limit: 20
}

docs {
  GET /remittances — the CQRS read side. Reads from Elasticsearch, never
  from Postgres; matches remittances where `accountId` is either the
  sender or the recipient.

  accountId is required — omitting it returns 400. There's no per-resource
  authorization layer yet (see CLAUDE.md), so requiring accountId at least
  stops this from defaulting to "every remittance in the system."

  Optional filters (all disabled by default above — enable and edit as
  needed): status (COMPLETED / REJECTED_COMPLIANCE / REJECTED_INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS
  / FAILED), from/to (ISO 8601 range on createdAt), limit (default 20).

  Eventually consistent: SendRemittanceUseCase publishes remittance.completed
  to Kafka only after its Postgres transaction commits, and a separate
  worker process (npm run worker:remittance-indexer) has to actually
  consume that event and index it into Elasticsearch before it shows up
  here — there can be a short delay, and nothing shows up at all if that
  worker isn't running. If this returns an empty list right after "Send
  Remittance," that worker is either not running or hasn't caught up yet
  — it's not a bug.

  Prerequisites (run in order):
    1. Account / Create Account (Sender)
    2. Auth / Login
    3. Remittance / Send Remittance — at least once, so there's something
       to find
    4. `npm run worker:remittance-indexer` running in a separate terminal
}
